 "protocol": "PERF-3a (2026-10-01): launch-configuration sweep of ISLA's fused geometry kernels on the GB300.\n\nThe fused region's forward runs BLOCK_N = 8 points x all S slices per program with 4 warps and the backward\nBLOCK_N = 4 (defaults tuned on an RTX 4090, kernel study 2026-09-13). ISLA-PERF-2 measured the backward at\n42 ms per step against a 4.6 ms forward at 200,000 cells x 256 slices (twelve layers), nine times the forward.\nThis sweeps (BLOCK_N, num_warps) for both kernels at the reporting shape (B=1, N=200,000, S=256, K=1, bf16\nautocast as in training) and reports median kernel time over 20 timed calls after 3 warm-ups, plus exactness\nagainst the default configuration: the per-point outputs (bias, mix, pooled) and the per-point gradients\n(logits, r, n_hat, d_hat) must be bitwise identical (the tile size does not change any per-point reduction);\nthe per-slice and per-weight gradients (z_pos, m_s, weight, bias) are summed over tiles in a different order\nand must agree to 1e-5 relative.\n\nUsage: python geo_kernel_sweep.py <out.json>\n",
